# Frontend (`apps/web`)

- React 19 + Vite + React Router (`react-router`, not `react-router-dom`).
- Styles: colocated CSS Modules (`.module.scss`). Do not add Tailwind or a second styling system.
- Domain types and form validation come from `@fleet-live/shared`. Do not re-declare vehicle schemas. `src/types/` is table generics (`table.ts`), not domain models.
- User-facing copy is German.

## Data

- HTTP only through `src/api/` (`client.ts` + resource modules). Components do not `fetch`.
- List state lives in the URL (`useVehicleListQuery`). Cache, prefetch, and SSE focus stay in hooks (`useVehicleList`, `useVehicleStream`).
- Live updates: existing EventSource + focus POST. Do not add polling or WebSockets.
- Handle loading, error, and not-found explicitly (see `VehicleDetailPage`).

## UI split

- `components/ui` stays generic (Table, Button, Modal, Avatar, Checkbox, Input). No vehicle fields there. Use those primitives everywhere (assignment, fleet picker, tables, login, registration, account, forms). Do not add raw `<input type="text|search|checkbox">` or one-off initial circles.
- Vehicle columns/filters belong in `components/vehicles/` (e.g. `vehicleTableConfig.tsx`). Alert columns/filters belong in `components/alerts/`. Driver columns belong in `components/drivers/`. The shift briefing lives on `/` (`BriefingPage`). Speed colour comes only from `speedBand` / `SPEED_BAND_COLORS`, not status greens.
- Prefer composition and local state. No new global store; `VehiclesProvider` already coordinates list epoch and telemetry overrides. Write actions (create/edit/delete, sim pause, resolve alerts, driver assignment, depot CRUD) are for `dispatcher`; `viewer` is read-only (including inbox, drivers, speed indicator, depot circles).
- No frontend unit-test runner. Do not add Jest/Vitest unless explicitly asked.

## Map

- Leaflet on the detail page (`VehicleMap`) and the fleet page (`FleetMap`); shared basemap/theme in `leafletMap.ts`.
- Marker at last telemetry. The detail-map trail is the **selected** trip: the open trip plus live `path_delta` while `DRIVING` and that open trip is selected; a selected closed trip draws its archived polyline (no live append). Decode with `decodePolyline`. SSE `path_delta` is road vertices, not the tick chord. `path_reset` replaces the trail (new trip), it does not append. Do not concatenate a closed `trip.path` with live crumbs. The trip table is paginated; list rows have no `path` — fetch `GET …/trips/:tripId` for the line.
- The marker slides along the new vertices (~400 ms). The trail grows with the marker, never ahead of it. The map stays centered on the vehicle until the user pans or zooms; "Fahrzeug zentrieren" resumes follow and keeps it.
- Status is not a form field and not a trip toggle.
- Do not fetch the telemetry history for the trail. That is the hot buffer and it rolls over mid-drive.
- No map on the list page. It shows only the current page and exposes the telemetry batching.
- Fleet map: markers and clusters, no trails. Snapshot via `GET /api/vehicles/positions` once per non-status filter or `drivers` change — pan, zoom, and plate search do not refetch. Plate or current-driver search lists matches from that snapshot; choosing one centers the map and opens the side panel, the status chip stays, and the other vehicles stay. A hit outside the chip is still drawn. Empty driver selection means the company snapshot, not “no markers”. Rows with `has_position: false` are not drawn. Status chips (Auf Fahrt, Standby, Feierabend, Kein Signal) filter that snapshot in the client and replace the fleet-map legend. Each chip shows `X im Ausschnitt / Y gesamt`. Y counts the filtered fleet with a position, so the four Y values sum to that count. Warnungen, Wenig Tank, Kein Fahrer, and Im Depot stay server filters and combine with the chip. Above `FLEET_POSITIONS_MAX` Y is the sum of density-cell `counts`, and a chip does not hide vehicles inside a mixed cell. `meta.without_position` is shown only when it is greater than 0; in positions mode that count opens the list of those vehicles. Points cluster locally through zoom 16. Zoom 17 draws the individual markers; the basemap may scale past its native tiles up to zoom 18. The index rebuilds when the vehicle set changes and at most once per several seconds when only coordinates change. A cluster click flies to the zoom where that cluster splits. Vehicles piled within 25 m also open the member list. The list stays until the user zooms back out or closes it. Cluster icons stay keyed by cluster id. The ring shows status counts; Kein Signal marks the cluster. Density mode above `FLEET_POSITIONS_MAX` draws cells, not a sample, and then has no per-vehicle rows for the without-position list. The side list is the bottom-left panel and only appears when the current view has at most 100 vehicles, so it never sits under Depots as a truncated dump of the company. The Fahrer control is a modal (`Modal` `size="lg"`) that searches drivers (one vehicle each, show plate) and applies with Übernehmen — not a dropdown, not a roster dump, not a status chip. The toolbar shows a summary on the trigger (name or count), never selected names as filter chips; add/remove only in the modal. Search shows the real match `total` and paginates (`page`); do not present `FLEET_DRIVERS_LIST_LIMIT` as the hit count. SSE focus is the `DRIVING` ids in the current view, capped at `STREAM_FOCUS_MAX_IDS`. A marker or list row selects the vehicle in the panel beside the map (plate, driver, status, speed, age of `recorded_at`, link to the detail page) and highlights that row. The panel does not cover the map. „Alle Fahrzeuge anzeigen“ fits the filtered fleet. The toolbar shows Live from the SSE connection (`connected` and `event: heartbeat`); `letzte Änderung vor X s` is only the age of the last patch. A dropped stream shows a fixed notice. Draw with a Leaflet canvas renderer — do not create thousands of DOM marker icons. Company depots are named circles (`GET /api/sites`); dispatcher edits them in `DepotPanel` (place, drag, radius). `Input` covers search and range sliders; do not add a raw `<input type="range">`.
- `components/ui` stays map-free.

## Domain copy

- Status labels live in `components/vehicles/vehicleStatus.ts`. Do not render the raw enum.
- Tempo in the list/detail uses `speedBand` from shared and `SPEED_BAND_COLORS` — not `VEHICLE_STATUS_COLORS`. Orange is over `speed_limit_kmh` without an open event; red is `speeding_open`. Inbox `/alerts` is warnings (Ereignis from `formatAlertEvent`, chips for open/resolved and `type`); `/drivers` is SPEEDING history (snapshot driver). Vehicle detail lists open LOW_FUEL / OFFLINE. `/` is the company shift briefing (KPI tiles + charts; deep-links into inbox / lists). The Warnungen nav shows the open inbox count.
- Timestamps from the API are naive UTC. Format them via `utils/dateTime.ts`, never print the raw string.
